==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|īsen}}, {{l|ang|īren}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*īsarną}}, probably from {{etyl|cel-pro|ang}} {{m|cel-pro|*īsarnom}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₁ésh₂r̥||blood}}. Cognates include {{cog|osx|īsarn}}, {{cog|nl|ijzer}}, {{cog|goh|īsarn}} ({{cog|de|Eisen}}), {{cog|non|ísarn}}, {{m|non|járn}} ({{cog|da|jern}} or {{m|da|jærn}}, {{cog|nb|jern}}, {{cog|nn|jarn}}, {{cog|sv|järn}}), {{cog|got|𐌴𐌹𐍃𐌰𐍂𐌽}}, {{cog|sga|īärn}} ({{cog|ga|iarann}}, {{cog|cy|haearn}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈiːzern/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|n|head=īsern|īsern}}

# the metal [[iron]]
# an instrument or tool made from iron, especially an iron [[sword]]
# an iron [[shackle]] or [[fetter]]

